data: {"invocationId":"e-9016d953-f080-4e75-8bdd-2850851213d0","author":"crucible","actions":{"stateDelta":{"intake":{"question":"Should we use an AI marketing tool to text all our past customers a fall tune-up promo?","leaning":"Yes, blast the whole list next week","profile":{"name":"","industry":"HVAC repair and installation","location":"Frederick, Maryland","size":"4 technicians","current_tools":["Housecall Pro","QuickBooks Online"],"budget":"$150/month","goals":["fill the fall schedule"],"constraints":""}},"evidence_mode":"web"},"artifactDelta":{},"requestedAuthConfigs":{},"requestedToolConfirmations":{}},"output":"Assemble the shared evidence for this decision: Should we use an AI marketing tool to text all our past customers a fall tune-up promo? (HVAC repair and installation, Frederick, Maryland)","nodeInfo":{"path":"crucible@1/intake@1","outputFor":["crucible@1/intake@1"]},"id":"91a51d79-a8a5-4a60-8866-421f66424b68","timestamp":1794351852.2576208}

data: {"modelVersion":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5","content":{"parts":[{"text":"I need to output JSON only, on one line with no markdown, and the search results contain links while the schema wants plain-text claims, so the URLs go only in the sources. Facts should be 6-12 items taken from the search results. I don't have any vendor pricing pages in the results, so I can't state pricing as verified and will need to flag it as an open question rather than invent figures. Could\n\nI'm considering whether to include pricing for vendors like Housecall Pro, but I have no verified pricing pages, so I'd rather flag it as unverified than guess at numbers. I'm also weighing Maryland and federal rules on telephone solicitation and contractor licensing, which would need to be checked against primary sources.\n\nI'm checking the timing rules next: quiet hours and the FCC consent rule, which I recall was vacated, along with how existing customer relationships are treated. I'll mark the general knowledge about Maryland's telephone and privacy laws as unverified and needing a check against primary sources.\n\nI'm noting that the outline is ready for the JSON, with the open questions covering list size, consent records, and team capacity still to be listed, so I can write it out now.\n\n","thought":true},{"text":"{\"decision\":\"Whether to use an AI marketing tool to text the entire past-customer list a fall tune-up promotion next week, rather than sending in smaller batches, using another channel, or not running the campaign.\",\"options\":[\"Do nothing: no promo campaign, rely on inbound calls, referrals and existing maintenance agreements.\",\"Blast the whole list by SMS next week through an AI marketing tool, as the owner leans.\",\"Run staged, segmented waves (agreement members, 12-24 month lapsed customers, aging systems), texting only customers with documented consent and emailing the rest, sized to open schedule slots, using Housecall Pro's built-in marketing features.\",\"Add a separate third-party AI reactivation platform to the stack, subject to the $150/month budget and a check that it connects to Housecall Pro.\"],\"facts\":[{\"claim\":\"Marketing texts generally require prior express written consent under TCPA rules. Businesses should confirm how and when each number was collected and whether the customer agreed to receive texts, and use email where consent is unclear. A TCPA violation is a legal risk for a whole-list blast to an older list.\",\"source\":\"https://www.usemetron.com/blog/reactivate-past-customers-with-ai\",\"verified\":true},{\"claim\":\"Texting businesses should register their number for A2P 10DLC so carriers deliver the messages, include clear opt-out instructions, honor opt-outs immediately, and avoid messaging the same customer more than a few times a year. Unregistered or complaint-heavy bulk texting risks carrier filtering.\",\"source\":\"https://www.usemetron.com/blog/reactivate-past-customers-with-ai\",\"verified\":true},{\"claim\":\"Housecall Pro, which the owner already uses, has an Automated Texts feature in its Marketing Center. It selects up to 10 past customers per day who look due, uses AI to write a personalized text from their service history, holds each message for a 3-day review window, and skips opted-out customers, customers with no valid mobile number, and anyone texted in the last 90 days. It is SMS-only and replies go to the Housecall Pro inbox. It is built for a steady trickle rather than a one-week blast of the whole list.\",\"source\":\"https://help.housecallpro.com/en/articles/16776745-automated-texts-how-ai-rebooks-your-past-customers\",\"verified\":true},{\"claim\":\"Reactivation guidance is to send 2-3 weeks before the slow period, in small waves sized to open capacity. The example given is that if you need 10 jobs and assume one in ten recipients books, you start with about 100 customers and watch replies for 48 hours before sending the next wave. The one-in-ten rate is an illustrative assumption, not a benchmark. A full-list blast risks overbooking a 4-technician team.\",\"source\":\"https://www.usemetron.com/blog/reactivate-past-customers-with-ai\",\"verified\":true},{\"claim\":\"Recommended HVAC segmentation is aging systems (12+ years), maintenance-agreement members with unused visits, recent inactive customers (12-24 months), and heat pump versus gas furnace splits. Each segment gets different messaging, and the guide says never to mix the cohorts in one prompt.\",\"source\":\"https://contractoraihub.com/guides/ai-hvac-seasonal-tune-up-campaigns\",\"verified\":true},{\"claim\":\"The same guide says AI-drafted copy must not invent discounts, promise free parts, diagnose problems, or use scare tactics. Pricing must come from the company's own pricing matrix and never be generated by AI. Sending should not be automated without human dispatch oversight, and customer phone numbers, addresses and gate codes should be stripped from prompts to third-party AI tools.\",\"source\":\"https://contractoraihub.com/guides/ai-hvac-seasonal-tune-up-campaigns\",\"verified\":true},{\"claim\":\"The guide recommends weather-triggered timing: an early-bird touch about 30 days before first freeze or heat wave, a reminder 7-10 days before a forecast overnight freeze (below 35°F), and route-density fill-ins for open technician gaps within about 3 miles. It argues timing matters more than copywriting. This is a vendor-content claim, not a measured benchmark.\",\"source\":\"https://contractoraihub.com/guides/ai-hvac-seasonal-tune-up-campaigns\",\"verified\":true},{\"claim\":\"Metron's reactivation guidance says effective messages are short, personal and specific, with one clear reason to book. It says generic big discounts can train customers to wait for sales, and that a specific reason to book often works better than a generic coupon. It suggests the 'recommended but not done' segment is often the most valuable.\",\"source\":\"https://www.usemetron.com/blog/reactivate-past-customers-with-ai\",\"verified\":true},{\"claim\":\"Other tools sell this category. ServiceTitan's marketing automation connects campaigns to scheduling so a text or email to membership customers can carry a booking link that places the job on the dispatch board. Ignitvio offers AI database-reactivation sequences that handle replies and book estimates to a calendar. Neither source retrieved here gives pricing.\",\"source\":\"https://www.servicetitan.com/guides/ai-automation-playbook/automating-marketing\",\"verified\":true},{\"claim\":\"No vendor pricing page was retrieved in this session for Housecall Pro, ServiceTitan, Ignitvio or others, so no current plan or monthly price is verified. Whether Automated Texts is included in the owner's current Housecall Pro plan or needs an upgrade or add-on must be confirmed on the vendor's pricing page or in the account.\",\"source\":\"\",\"verified\":false},{\"claim\":\"Federal TCPA rules also restrict calling hours for telemarketing (generally 8am-9pm recipient local time) and allow statutory damages per message, so consent records matter. Maryland has its own telephone solicitation and consumer-protection rules, such as the Stop the Spam Calls Act of 2023, that may be stricter than federal rules. Their exact application to an HVAC company texting existing customers was not confirmed by search.\",\"source\":\"\",\"verified\":false},{\"claim\":\"In Maryland, HVACR work requires state licensing through the State Board of HVACR Contractors. Advertising typically must include the license number, and residential contractors may also fall under Maryland Home Improvement Commission rules, so promo copy should be checked for required license disclosures. Frederick County or city rules were not checked by search.\",\"source\":\"\",\"verified\":false}],\"open_questions\":[\"How many customers are on the list, and how was each phone number collected? Is there documented consent to receive marketing texts, or only service-related contact?\",\"Is the business's texting number registered for A2P 10DLC, and does Housecall Pro handle that registration?\",\"Does the owner's current Housecall Pro plan include Automated Texts or campaign texting, and what do additional SMS credits or an upgrade cost against the $150/month budget?\",\"How many tune-up slots does the 4-technician team have open this fall, and how many bookings can it absorb per week without hurting repair and install work?\",\"What is the actual offer (discount, price, or priority booking), and does the margin hold at the intended price?\",\"How many customers are active maintenance-agreement members versus one-time repair customers, and when was each last serviced?\",\"Has Maryland counsel or the company's attorney confirmed whether Maryland rules add consent, timing or disclosure requirements beyond federal TCPA for this kind of text?\",\"What response and booking rates has the company seen from past email or text outreach, and what are local benchmarks for tune-up conversion?\",\"Given the search date of November 10, is the 'fall' window already late, so that a staged rollout or weather-triggered timing would meaningfully change results?\"]}"}],"role":"model"},"partial":false,"finishReason":"STOP","usageMetadata":{"cachedContentTokenCount":0,"candidatesTokenCount":3612,"promptTokenCount":5141,"thoughtsTokenCount":1044,"totalTokenCount":8753},"invocationId":"e-9016d953-f080-4e75-8bdd-2850851213d0","author":"researcher","actions":{"stateDelta":{"evidence":{"decision":"Whether to use an AI marketing tool to text the entire past-customer list a fall tune-up promotion next week, rather than sending in smaller batches, using another channel, or not running the campaign.","options":["Do nothing: no promo campaign, rely on inbound calls, referrals and existing maintenance agreements.","Blast the whole list by SMS next week through an AI marketing tool, as the owner leans.","Run staged, segmented waves (agreement members, 12-24 month lapsed customers, aging systems), texting only customers with documented consent and emailing the rest, sized to open schedule slots, using Housecall Pro's built-in marketing features.","Add a separate third-party AI reactivation platform to the stack, subject to the $150/month budget and a check that it connects to Housecall Pro."],"facts":[{"claim":"Marketing texts generally require prior express written consent under TCPA rules. Businesses should confirm how and when each number was collected and whether the customer agreed to receive texts, and use email where consent is unclear. A TCPA violation is a legal risk for a whole-list blast to an older list.","source":"https://www.usemetron.com/blog/reactivate-past-customers-with-ai","verified":true},{"claim":"Texting businesses should register their number for A2P 10DLC so carriers deliver the messages, include clear opt-out instructions, honor opt-outs immediately, and avoid messaging the same customer more than a few times a year. Unregistered or complaint-heavy bulk texting risks carrier filtering.","source":"https://www.usemetron.com/blog/reactivate-past-customers-with-ai","verified":true},{"claim":"Housecall Pro, which the owner already uses, has an Automated Texts feature in its Marketing Center. It selects up to 10 past customers per day who look due, uses AI to write a personalized text from their service history, holds each message for a 3-day review window, and skips opted-out customers, customers with no valid mobile number, and anyone texted in the last 90 days. It is SMS-only and replies go to the Housecall Pro inbox. It is built for a steady trickle rather than a one-week blast of the whole list.","source":"https://help.housecallpro.com/en/articles/16776745-automated-texts-how-ai-rebooks-your-past-customers","verified":true},{"claim":"Reactivation guidance is to send 2-3 weeks before the slow period, in small waves sized to open capacity. The example given is that if you need 10 jobs and assume one in t