commended but not done' segment is often the most valuable.","source":"https://www.usemetron.com/blog/reactivate-past-customers-with-ai","verified":true},{"claim":"Other tools sell this category. ServiceTitan's marketing automation connects campaigns to scheduling so a text or email to membership customers can carry a booking link that places the job on the dispatch board. Ignitvio offers AI database-reactivation sequences that handle replies and book estimates to a calendar. Neither source retrieved here gives pricing.","source":"https://www.servicetitan.com/guides/ai-automation-playbook/automating-marketing","verified":true},{"claim":"No vendor pricing page was retrieved in this session for Housecall Pro, ServiceTitan, Ignitvio or others, so no current plan or monthly price is verified. Whether Automated Texts is included in the owner's current Housecall Pro plan or needs an upgrade or add-on must be confirmed on the vendor's pricing page or in the account.","source":"","verified":false},{"claim":"Federal TCPA rules also restrict calling hours for telemarketing (generally 8am-9pm recipient local time) and allow statutory damages per message, so consent records matter. Maryland has its own telephone solicitation and consumer-protection rules, such as the Stop the Spam Calls Act of 2023, that may be stricter than federal rules. Their exact application to an HVAC company texting existing customers was not confirmed by search.","source":"","verified":false},{"claim":"In Maryland, HVACR work requires state licensing through the State Board of HVACR Contractors. Advertising typically must include the license number, and residential contractors may also fall under Maryland Home Improvement Commission rules, so promo copy should be checked for required license disclosures. Frederick County or city rules were not checked by search.","source":"","verified":false}],"open_questions":["How many customers are on the list, and how was each phone number collected? Is there documented consent to receive marketing texts, or only service-related contact?","Is the business's texting number registered for A2P 10DLC, and does Housecall Pro handle that registration?","Does the owner's current Housecall Pro plan include Automated Texts or campaign texting, and what do additional SMS credits or an upgrade cost against the $150/month budget?","How many tune-up slots does the 4-technician team have open this fall, and how many bookings can it absorb per week without hurting repair and install work?","What is the actual offer (discount, price, or priority booking), and does the margin hold at the intended price?","How many customers are active maintenance-agreement members versus one-time repair customers, and when was each last serviced?","Has Maryland counsel or the company's attorney confirmed whether Maryland rules add consent, timing or disclosure requirements beyond federal TCPA for this kind of text?","What response and booking rates has the company seen from past email or text outreach, and what are local benchmarks for tune-up conversion?","Given the search date of November 10, is the 'fall' window already late, so that a staged rollout or weather-triggered timing would meaningfully change results?"]}},"artifactDelta":{},"requestedAuthConfigs":{},"requestedToolConfirmations":{}},"output":{"decision":"Whether to use an AI marketing tool to text the entire past-customer list a fall tune-up promotion next week, rather than sending in smaller batches, using another channel, or not running the campaign.","options":["Do nothing: no promo campaign, rely on inbound calls, referrals and existing maintenance agreements.","Blast the whole list by SMS next week through an AI marketing tool, as the owner leans.","Run staged, segmented waves (agreement members, 12-24 month lapsed customers, aging systems), texting only customers with documented consent and emailing the rest, sized to open schedule slots, using Housecall Pro's built-in marketing features.","